    "text": "III ID FEBRUARII: NATALE SANCTE EUFRASI\u00e6 VIRGINIS.\nSVM WER W\u00c6S ON ALEXANDRIA M\u00c6G\u00d0E PAFNVNTIVS genemned, se w\u00e6s eallum mannum\n\u00dea w\u00e6s hire wer \u00feearle gedrefed for\u00feam him nan bearn n\u00e6s gem\u00e6ne, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00e6fter his for\u00f0si\u00f0e to his \u00e6htum\nAnd gelomlice heo cyrcan sohte, and mid halsungum God w\u00e6s biddende \u00fe\u00e6t he him sum bearn forgeafe,\nAnd he sylf eac ferde geond manige stowa, gif he weninga hwilcne godes man findan mihte \u00fe\u00e6t his\n\u00dea \u00e6t nyhstan becom he to sumum mynstre; \u00fe\u00e6s mynstres f\u00e6der w\u00e6s swy\u00f0e m\u00e6re beforan Gode.\nAnd he \u00fea micelne d\u00e6l feos \u00feider ingesealde, and miccle \u00feeodr\u00e6dene nam to \u00feam abbode, and to \u00feam\nSe abbod \u00fea him efnsargode, and b\u00e6d God geornlice \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00feam \u00feegne forgeafe bearnes w\u00e6stm.\n\u00dea gehyrde god heora begra bene, and forgeaf him ane dohtor.\nMid \u00fey Pafnuntius geseah \u00fe\u00e6s abbodes m\u00e6ran drohtnunge, he seldan of \u00feam mynstre gewat; eac\n\u00dea \u00fe\u00e6t cild w\u00e6s seofon wintre, \u00fea letan hi hi fullian, and nemdon hi Eufrosina.\n\u00dea wurdon hire yldran swi\u00f0lice geblissode \u00feurh hi, for\u00feam heo w\u00e6s Gode andfencge, and wlytig on\nAnd mid \u00fey heo w\u00e6s twelf wintre, \u00fea gewat hire modor.\nSe f\u00e6der \u00fea gel\u00e6rde \u00fe\u00e6t m\u00e6den mid halgum gewirtum, and godcundum r\u00e6dingum, and mid eallum\n\u00dea asprang hire hlisa and wisdom and gel\u00e6rednys, geond ealle \u00fea ceastre, for\u00feam heo w\u00e6s on \u00feeawum\n\u00dea \u00e6t nyxtan com him an \u00feegen to, se w\u00e6s weligra and wur\u00fera \u00feonne ealle \u00fea o\u00fere, and hire to him\n\u00dea onfeng se f\u00e6der his wedd, and hi him behet.\n\u00dea \u00e6fter micelre tide \u00fea heo eahtatyne wyntre w\u00e6s, \u00fea genam se feder hi mid him to \u00fe\u00e6re stowe, \u00fee he\nAnd cw\u00e6\u00f0 to \u00feam abbode, Ic h\u00e6bbe broht hider \u00feone w\u00e6stm \u00feinra gebeda, mine dohtor, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu hire\n\u00d0a het se abbod hi l\u00e6dan to spr\u00e6chuse, and lange hwile wi\u00f0 hi spr\u00e6c and l\u00e6rde hi cl\u00e6nnysse and\nAnd heo \u00fea wunode \u00fe\u00e6r seofon dagas, and geornlice hlyste \u00fe\u00e6ra bro\u00f0ra sanges, and heora drohtnunga\nAnd heo wear\u00f0 bihydig be \u00feissum.\n\u00dea \u00fey \u00f0riddan d\u00e6ge cw\u00e6\u00f0 Pafnuntius to \u00feam abbode, Gang f\u00e6der \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fein \u00feeowen \u00f0e m\u00e6ge gegretan,\n\u00dea se abbod com, \u00fea feoll heo to his fotum and cw\u00e6\u00f0, F\u00e6der gebide for me \u00fe\u00e6t God mine sawle him\n\u00dea a\u00feenode se abbod his hand, and hi gebletsode and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Drihten God, \u00feu \u00fee oncneowe Adam \u00e6r he\nHi \u00fea \u00e6fter \u00feissum wordum ham ferdon.\nW\u00e6s his gewuna Pafnuntius \u00fe\u00e6t swa oft swa him \u00e6nig munuc to com, \u00feonne l\u00e6dde he hine into his\n\u00dea gelamp hit embe geares ryne, \u00fe\u00e6t hit w\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6s abbodes hadingd\u00e6g.\n\u00dea sende anne bro\u00f0or to Pafnuntie, and la\u00feode hine to \u00fe\u00e6re symbelnysse.\n\u00dea se munuc to his healle com, \u00fea ne funde he hine \u00e6t ham.\nMid\u00fey \u00fea Eufrosina \u00feone munuc \u00fe\u00e6r wiste, \u00fea gecigde heo hine to hire and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Sege me bro\u00feor for\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he, \u00fereo hund muneca and twa and fiftig.\nHeo \u00fea git axode and cw\u00e6\u00f0, gif hwilc \u00feider in bugan wile, wile eower abbod hine underfon?\nGea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he, ac mid eallum gefean he hine underfeh\u00f0 swi\u00f0or for \u00fe\u00e6re drihtenlican stefne \u00fee \u00feus\nSinga\u00f0 ge ealle cw\u00e6\u00f0 heo on anre cyrcan, and f\u00e6sta\u00f0 ge ealle gelice?\nSe bro\u00feor cw\u00e6\u00f0, Ealle we singa\u00f0 gem\u00e6nelice \u00e6tg\u00e6dere, ac ure \u00e6ghwilc f\u00e6st be \u00feam \u00fee him to\n\u00d0a heo \u00fea ealle heora drohtnunga asmead h\u00e6fde, \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0 heo, Ic wolde gecyrran to \u00feyllicre\nSe bro\u00feor cw\u00e6\u00f0, Eala swustor, ne ge\u00feafa \u00f0u \u00fe\u00e6t \u00e6nig man \u00feinne lichaman besmite; ne ne syle \u00feu \u00feinne\nAc far nu to mynstre digellice, and alege \u00feine woruldlican gegyrlan, and gegyre \u00fee mid munucreafe;\n\u00dea gelicode hire \u00feeos spr\u00e6c, and heo \u00fea to him cw\u00e6\u00f0, Ac hwa m\u00e6g me beefesian.\nSo\u00f0lice ic nolde \u00fe\u00e6t hit \u00fea dydon \u00fee n\u00e6nne geleafan nabba\u00f0 to Gode.\nSe bro\u00feor hyre to cw\u00e6\u00fe, Loca nu, \u00fein f\u00e6der sceal mid me to mynstre, and bi\u00fe \u00fe\u00e6r \u00fery dagas o\u00f0\u00f0e\nOngemang \u00feissum, com ham Pafnuntius, and swa he \u00feone munuc geseah, \u00fea axode he hine to hwi he\n\u00dea s\u00e6de he him \u00fe\u00e6t hit w\u00e6re \u00fe\u00e6s abbodes hadungd\u00e6g, and he to him cuman sceolde mid him to his\nPafnuntius \u00fea wear\u00f0 geblissod swi\u00f0e, and sona mid him \u00feam bro\u00feor ferde to mynstre.\nOngemang \u00feisum sende Eufrosina anne cniht swi\u00f0e getrywne hire to \u00feam mynstre, and b\u00e6d \u00fe\u00e6t swa\n\u00dea lamp hit \u00feurh Godes mildheortnysse, gemette he an \u00feara muneca wi\u00f0utan \u00feam mynstre.\n\u00dea se cniht b\u00e6d hine \u00fe\u00e6t he come mid him to Eufrosinan.\n\u00dea he to hire com, \u00fea grette heo hine and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Gebide for me.\nHe \u00fea for hi geb\u00e6d, and hi gebletsode, and wi\u00f0 hi ges\u00e6t.\nHeo \u00fea cw\u00e6\u00f0 to him, Hlaford, ic h\u00e6bbe Cristenne f\u00e6der, and so\u00f0ne Godes \u00feeow, and he h\u00e6f\u00f0 myccle\nNu wile min f\u00e6der for his idlum welum me were syllan, ac ic nolde n\u00e6fre me sylfe \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6t\nAnd ic ne dear beon minum f\u00e6der ungehyrsum, and ic nat hw\u00e6t ic be \u00feysum don m\u00e6g.\nEalle \u00feas niht witodlice ic ane wunode, God biddende \u00fe\u00e6t he minre earman sawle his myltse \u00e6tywe,\nNu bidde ic \u00f0e for \u00feam edleane \u00feinre sawle \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu me wisige to \u00feam \u00feingum, \u00fee to Gode gelumpon.\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 se bro\u00f0or, Drihten cw\u00e6\u00f0 on his godspelle, swa hwa swa ne wi\u00fes\u00e6c\u00f0 f\u00e6der and meder and\nNat ic hw\u00e6t ic \u00fee mare secge; swa\u00feeh gif \u00feu m\u00e6ge \u00fea costnunga \u00feines fl\u00e6sces ar\u00e6fnan, \u00feonne forl\u00e6t\n\u00deines f\u00e6der \u00e6hta finda\u00f0 yrfeweardes genoge.\n\u00de\u00e6t m\u00e6den him to cw\u00e6\u00f0, Ic getrywe on Godes fultum and on \u00feinne, \u00fe\u00e6t ic becume to mire sawla\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 se bro\u00f0or, Ne scealt \u00feu na \u00feyllice gewilnunga l\u00e6tan aslacian, eornostlice \u00feu wast \u00fe\u00e6t hit is\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 heo, for\u00fey ic gela\u00f0ode \u00fee hyder, \u00fe\u00e6t ic wolde \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u me bletsodest and me sy\u00f0\u00f0an feaxe\nSe bro\u00f0or \u00fea hi gegyrede mid munucreafe, and hi bletsode and \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0, Drihten, se \u00fee alysde his\nHe \u00fea \u00e6fter \u00feyssum, mid blisse ham ferde, God wuldrigende.\nEufrosina \u00fea \u00feohte \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00feende, Gif ic nu fare to f\u00e6mnena mynstre, \u00feonne sec\u00f0 min f\u00e6der me \u00fe\u00e6r,\nHeo \u00fea \u00feone wiflican gegyrlan hire ofdyde, and hi gescrydde mid werlicum, and on \u00e6fentid gewat of\n\u00dea \u00fe\u00e6s on mergen com Pafnuntius to \u00fe\u00e6re ceastre, and \u00fea \u00e6fter Godes willan eode he into cyrcan.\nEufrosina betwux \u00feysum becom to \u00feam mynstre \u00fee hire f\u00e6der to sohte.\n\u00dea eode se geatweard to \u00feam abbode and cw\u00e6\u00f0 him to.\nF\u00e6der her is cumen an eunuchus of cinges hirede wilna\u00f0 \u00feinre spr\u00e6ce.\nSe abbod \u00fea uteode, and heo sona feoll to his fotum, and onfangenre bletsunge hi tog\u00e6dere ges\u00e6ton.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se abbod, Bearn for hwilcum \u00feingum come \u00feu hider.\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 heo, Ic w\u00e6s on cinges hirede, and ic eom eunuchus, and ic symle wilnode to munuclicum\nNu geaxode ic eowre m\u00e6ran drohtnunge, and min willa is \u00fe\u00e6t ic mid eow eardian mote, gif eower\nIc h\u00e6bbe m\u00e6nigfealde \u00e6hta, and gif me her God reste forgifen wile, Ic gedo \u00fe\u00e6t hi cuma\u00f0 hider.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se abbod, Wel come \u00feu min bearn; efne \u00feis is ure mynster, wuna her mid us gif \u00fee licige.\n\u00dea axode he hine hw\u00e6t his nama w\u00e6re.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he, Smaragdus ic eom geciged.\nSe abbod him to cw\u00e6\u00f0, \u00feu eart geong, ne miht \u00feu ane wunian, ac \u00feu behofast \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu h\u00e6bbe \u00feone \u00fee\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 he, Ic do min f\u00e6der \u00e6fter \u00feinum wordum.\nHe \u00fea for\u00f0teah \u00fea fiftig mancsas, and \u00feam abbode sealde and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Nim f\u00e6der \u00feis feoh for\u00f0on, and\n\u00dea gecigde se abbod ane bro\u00feor to him se w\u00e6s genemned Agapitus, haliges lifes man, and wur\u00f0ful on\nAgapitus \u00fea underfeng hine on his cytan.\n\u00dea for\u00feam se sylfe Smaragdus w\u00e6s wlitig on ansyne, swa oft swa \u00f0a bro\u00f0ra comon to cyrcan, \u00feonne\nAnd he \u00fea gecigde Smaragdum to him and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Min bearn \u00fein ansyn is wlitig, and \u00feissum bro\u00ferum\nNu wille ic \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu sitte \u00fee sylf on \u00feire cytan, and singe \u00fe\u00e6r \u00feine tida, and \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6rinne gereorde; nelle\nAnd he \u00fea bebead Agapito \u00fe\u00e6t he gegearwode \u00e6ne emptige cytan, and Smaragdum \u00feider inne\nAgapitus \u00fea gefylde \u00fe\u00e6t his abbod him bebead, and gel\u00e6dde smaragdum into \u00fe\u00e6re westan cytan, \u00fe\u00e6r\nPafnuntius \u00fea witodlice, hire f\u00e6der, \u00fea he ham com ofestlice eode inn to \u00feam bure \u00fee his dohtor inne\n\u00dea cw\u00e6don hi, to niht we hi gesawon, ac we nyston on mergen hw\u00e6r heo becom; \u00fea wendon we \u00fe\u00e6t\nHe \u00fea sende to \u00feam brydguman, and hi axode \u00fe\u00e6r, ac heo \u00fe\u00e6r n\u00e6s.\n\u00dea hira brydguma gehyrde \u00fe\u00e6t heo losad w\u00e6s, \u00fea wear\u00f0 he swi\u00f0e gedrefed, com \u00fea to Pafnuntio, and\n\u00dea s\u00e6don sume, be weninga sum man hi beswac, and hi aweg al\u00e6dde.\nHe \u00fea sende ridende men geond ealle Alexandria land and Egypta, and hi sohton betwux scipli\u00feende,\nSe sweor bem\u00e6nde his snore, and se brydguma his bryd.\nSe f\u00e6der his dohtor beweop and cw\u00e6\u00f0, wa me, mine sweteste bearn, wa me, mira eagena leoht and\nHwa bereafode me minra speda o\u00f0\u00f0e tostencte mine \u00e6hta?\nHwa forcearf minne wingeard, o\u00f0\u00f0e hwa adw\u00e6scte min leohtf\u00e6t?\nHwa bescirede me mines hihtes, o\u00fe\u00fee hwa gewemde \u00feone wlite mire dohtor?\nHwilc wulf gel\u00e6hte min lamb, o\u00fe\u00fee hwylc stow on s\u00e6 o\u00f0\u00f0e on lande h\u00e6f\u00f0 behyd swa cynelice\nHeo w\u00e6s geomrigendra frofor, and geswencendra rest.\nEala \u00feu eor\u00fee ne swelh \u00feu n\u00e6fre min blod, \u00e6r ic geseo hw\u00e6t sy gedon be Eufrosinan mire dehter.\nGehyredum \u00feysum wordum hi ongunnon ealle weopan, and mycel heof w\u00e6s geond ealle \u00fea ceastre.\n\u00dea ne mihte Pafnuntius nan forebyrd habban, ne nane frofre onfon, ferde \u00fea to \u00feam abbode and feoll to\nWitodlice ic nat hw\u00e6r min dohtor is becumen.\n\u00dea se abbod \u00feis gehyrde, \u00fea wear\u00f0 he swy\u00f0e unbli\u00f0e, het \u00fea gesomnian ealle \u00fea gebro\u00f0ra to him and\n\u00c6tywa\u00f0 nu \u00fea so\u00fean lufan urum frynd.\nAnd gem\u00e6nelice biddan we God \u00fe\u00e6t he hine gemedemige to \u00e6tywenne hw\u00e6t sy gedon be his dehter.\nHi \u00fea ealle wucan f\u00e6stan, and on heora gebedum \u00feurhwunodon, ac him nan swutelung ne com swa\nWitodlice \u00fe\u00e6re eadigan femnan Eufrosinan ben w\u00e6s to Gode d\u00e6ges and nihtes, \u00fe\u00e6t heo n\u00e6fre on hire\n\u00d0a \u00feam abbode and \u00feam gebro\u00f0rum nan swutelung ne com, \u00fea frefrode he hine and cw\u00e6\u00f0, Bearn ne\nHu miccle ma m\u00e6g \u00feire dehter gelimpan \u00e6nig \u00feing butan Godes dihte?\nIc wat \u00fe\u00e6t heo sumne godne r\u00e6d hire geceas, for\u00fey us be hire nan \u00feincg ateowod w\u00e6s; and gif hit \u00fe\u00e6t\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 he gehyrt \u00feurh \u00feas word, and God herigende ham ferde, and hine abysgode on godum\n\u00dea sume d\u00e6ge com he eft to \u00feam abbode and cw\u00e6\u00fe, Gebide for me, for\u00feam min sar be mire dehter ma\nSe abbod \u00fea efensargiende him cw\u00e6\u00f0, woldest \u00feu spr\u00e6can wi\u00f0 anne bro\u00f0or se com of \u00fe\u00e6s cynges\nFor\u00feam he nyste \u00fe\u00e6t heo w\u00e6s his dohtor.\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 he \u00fe\u00e6t he georne wolde.\nSe abbod \u00fea het Agapitum \u00fe\u00e6t he hine l\u00e6dde into Smaragdo \u00feam bre\u00feer.\n\u00dea heo \u00fea on hire f\u00e6der beseah, \u00fea wear\u00f0 heo eall mid tearum geondgoten, and he wende \u00fe\u00e6t hit w\u00e6re\nAnd heo hire heafod behylede mid hire culan, \u00fe\u00e6t he hi gecnawen ne sceolde, and \u00fea geendodum\n\u00dea ongan heo him to spr\u00e6can be heofona rices eadignysse, and hu se ingang begiten bi\u00f0 mid\nAnd heo cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fea git, Gelyf me ne forsih\u00f0 \u00fee na God; and gif \u00fein dohtor on \u00e6nigum lyre feallen\nAc getryw on God \u00fe\u00e6t heo sumne gode r\u00e6d hire geceas.\nL\u00e6t nu \u00feine micclan cwylminge; Agapitus min lareow me rehte \u00fee be \u00fee hu swy\u00f0e \u00feu gedrefed eart\nNu wylle ic sylfe eac, \u00feeah ic wac sy and synful, God biddan \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00fee forgife forebyrd and ge\u00feyld,\nGelomlice ic wilnode \u00fee geseonne \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu sume frofre \u00feurh me ea\u00f0modre findan mihtest.\nAnd heo \u00f0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 to him, Gang nu, min hlaford.\nPafnuntius \u00fea wear\u00f0 micclan gestrangod \u00feurh hire trymennesse, and fram hire gewat, and to \u00feam\nAnd hine \u00feam abbode and \u00feam bro\u00ferum bef\u00e6ste to gebedr\u00e6dene, and ham ferde God herigende.\n\u00dea gefylde Smaragdus on \u00fe\u00e6re netennysse, eahta and \u00feryttig wintra, and befeoll on untrumnysse and\n\u00dea com Pafnuntius eft to mynstre, and \u00e6fter \u00fe\u00e6s abbodes spr\u00e6ce and \u00feara bro\u00fera he b\u00e6d \u00fe\u00e6t he moste\n\u00dea het se abbod hine \u00feider l\u00e6dan.\nPafnuntius \u00fea ges\u00e6t wi\u00f0 him swa seocan, and wepende him to cw\u00e6\u00f0, Wa me hw\u00e6r synd nu \u00feine behat\nEfne nu we h\u00e6fdon sume frofre \u00feurh \u00fee, and \u00feu wylt us forl\u00e6tan.\nWa me, hwa sceal mine yldo afrefrian, to hwam sceal ic gan \u00fe\u00e6t me fultumige?\nMin sar is getwyfyld.\nNu hit is for eahta and \u00ferytti\u00f0an gearan \u00fe\u00e6t min dohtor me losode, and me nan swutelung ne com, \u00feeh\nMe hylt unar\u00e6fnedlic sar, to hwam m\u00e6g ic heononfor\u00f0 gehyltan, o\u00f0\u00f0e hwilce frofre m\u00e6g ic onfon.\nEallunga \u00feus heofende ic to helle ni\u00f0erstige.\nSmaragdus \u00fea geseonde \u00fe\u00e6t he nanre frofre onfon nolde, cw\u00e6\u00f0 to him, To hwi eart \u00f0u \u00feus swy\u00f0e\nCwyst \u00feu \u00fe\u00e6t Drihtnes hand sy unstrang, o\u00fe\u00fee him sy \u00e6nig \u00feing earfo\u00f0lic?\nGesete nu ende \u00feinre gedrefednysse, and gemun hu God geswutelode Iacobe \u00feam heahf\u00e6der Iosep his\nAc ic bidde \u00fee \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu \u00ferym dagum me ne forl\u00e6te.\nPafnuntius \u00fea anbidode \u00feara \u00fereora daga f\u00e6c \u00feus cwe\u00f0ende, Weninga God him h\u00e6f\u00f0 be me sum \u00feing\nAnd \u00fea on \u00feam \u00feryddan d\u00e6ge cw\u00e6\u00f0 he to him, Ic anbidode bro\u00feor \u00feas \u00fery dagas.\n\u00dea onget Sm